# Localization Rule — No Hardcoded Player-Facing Strings

All text visible to the player must use `Loc.Get(LocKeys.*)` or an equivalent localization helper. **Never hardcode human-readable strings in UI code.**

## Bad — PROHIBITED

```csharp
title.text = "Store";
button.text = "Buy";
label.text = "Locked";
effectText.text = $"+{val}% Quality";
lines.Add("Contract complete");
```

## Good — REQUIRED

```csharp
title.text  = Loc.Get(LocKeys.TiendaTitle);
button.text = Loc.Get(LocKeys.ContractClaim);
label.text  = Loc.Get(LocKeys.InstLocked);
effectText.text = Loc.Format(LocKeys.UpgradeEffectQuality, val);
lines.Add(Loc.Get(LocKeys.PremiereContractDone));
```

## Workflow for new strings

1. Add a `public const string MyKey = "my.key";` to `LocKeys.cs`
2. Add translations for `es`, `en`, `fr`, `de`, `ja` in `Loc.cs` (`BaseEs()` + each language override)
3. Use `Loc.Get(LocKeys.MyKey)` or `Loc.Format(LocKeys.MyKey, arg0, ...)` in UI code
4. If the panel rebuilds on language change: subscribe in `Awake()` and unsubscribe in `OnDestroy()`:
   ```csharp
   UserPrefs.OnLanguageChanged += RefreshLocalization;
   ```

## Helpers already available

- `GenreLoc.GetLabel(genre)` — localized genre names
- `ProductionLoc.GetRarityLabel(rarity)` — localized rarity labels
- `DepartmentLoc.GetName(type)` — localized department names
- `PremiereLoc.FormatMoneyReward(amount)` — localized money reward
- `Loc.Format(key, args...)` — format string with args

## Applies to all future screens

Store, Monetization, Supporter Packs, Ads, Boosts, Events, Settings, any new panel.
